From: Dena.emu <noreply@dena.emu>
Subject: arm64: dts: sun50i-h616: add the DE3 SRAM section for the display bus

The display engine bus claims SRAM C through allwinner,sram, but sram_c in
sun50i-h616.dtsi is the plain mmio-sram node with no section under it, so
sunxi_sram_of_parse() finds no matching section and the bus probe fails
with -EINVAL ("Couldn't map SRAM to device"): no DRM display on the H700.
Add the section like the H6 dtsi does and point the bus at it.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
@@ -163,7 +163,7 @@
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-de33",
 				     "allwinner,sun50i-a64-de2";
 			reg = <0x1000000 0x400000>;
-			allwinner,sram = <&sram_c 1>;
+			allwinner,sram = <&de3_sram 1>;
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <1>;
 			ranges = <0 0x1000000 0x400000>;
@@ -271,6 +271,12 @@
 				#address-cells = <1>;
 				#size-cells = <1>;
 				ranges = <0 0x00028000 0x30000>;
+
+				de3_sram: sram-section@0 {
+					compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-sram-c",
+						     "allwinner,sun50i-a64-sram-c";
+					reg = <0x0000 0x1e000>;
+				};
 			};
 		};
 
